        "heading": "The Shared Responsibility Split, Visually",
        "content": "The table above lists every layer of the stack, but the question an analyst actually asks mid-triage is simpler than a table: given this service model, is this specific layer the provider's job or the customer's? The diagram below compresses that lookup into a single glance. Notice that identity and data always land in the customer's column no matter which service model you are looking at — that column never shrinks to zero, and it is exactly where the breach almost always happened. When you are unsure which side of the line an incident falls on, trace the service model down to its outcome here before you write your root-cause conclusion.",
        "codeExample": "flowchart TD\n  A[\"Which service model?\"] --> B[\"IaaS - a bare VM\"]\n  A --> C[\"PaaS - managed app or database\"]\n  A --> D[\"SaaS - M365 or Salesforce\"]\n  B --> E[\"Provider: hardware + hypervisor\\nCustomer: OS, patching, identity, data\"]\n  C --> F[\"Provider: hardware + OS + runtime\\nCustomer: app code, identity, data\"]\n  D --> G[\"Provider: nearly everything\\nCustomer: identity, config, data\"]"
